	(descr "TDK (EPCOS) B82726S2163N030 current-compensated ring-core double choke, 250VAC/16A, 2.2mH/winding. Land pattern hand-built from the official TDK dimensional drawing (tdk-electronics.tdk.com/inf/30/db/ind_2008/b82726s2163.pdf, page 3 'Dimensional drawing and pin configuration', April 2025 revision): pin 1/2 (top row) on 18+/-0.4mm pitch, pin 4/3 (bottom row) on 38+/-0.3mm pitch, row-to-row (1/2 row to 4/3 row) pitch 23+/-0.2mm, lead diameter 1.6+/-0.1mm. Toroid body 50mm max diameter x 49mm max (side-elevation view in the datasheet; the datasheet does not give a top-down silhouette, so the F.Fab/F.CrtYd circle here is a CONSERVATIVE placement covering the lead footprint's centroid at the datasheet's stated max diameter -- verify true keep-out against the physical part / TDK's 3D model before fabrication). PAD NUMBERING matches TDK's own pin numbers 1-4 (no remapping): footprint pads 1-4 = atopile CommonModeChoke pins 1-4 directly (winding 1 = pads 1+4, winding 2 = pads 2+3). Datasheet states 'No polarity' -- the two windings are symmetric so there is no dot/phasing convention to respect.")
	(tags "common mode choke CMC B82726S TDK EPCOS EMI toroid")
